            <h2 style="color:#f9fafb;border-bottom-color:#374151;">FAQ</h2>
            <div itemscope itemprop="hasPart" itemtype="https://schema.org/Question" style="margin-bottom:24px;">
                <h3 itemprop="name" style="color:#f9fafb;font-size:1.05rem;margin:0 0 8px;">Q: What does an AI-generated ecommerce listing image set cost per SKU?</h3>
                <div itemprop="acceptedAnswer" itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer"><p style="color:#d1d5db;margin:0;">Roughly 100–140 list credits per SKU for the full English set. Across twelve SKUs the month runs: white-background heroes at 6 each (1K transparent), two feature infographics and one spec chart at 24 each (Qwen 3 Pro 2K), and two lifestyle shots at 9 each — plus the localized overlays and hero videos shared across the catalog. Twelve complete listings price inside a 3,624-credit month (2,282 on Ultra at 63%), not per-SKU invoices.</p></div>
            </div>
            <div itemscope itemprop="hasPart" itemtype="https://schema.org/Question" style="margin-bottom:24px;">
                <h3 itemprop="name" style="color:#f9fafb;font-size:1.05rem;margin:0 0 8px;">Q: How do you meet the marketplace''s pure-white main image rule?</h3>
                <div itemprop="acceptedAnswer" itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer"><p style="color:#d1d5db;margin:0;">By generating a clean cutout and compositing it yourself. The <code>background=transparent</code> flag on GPT Image 2.5 Flare is 1K-only at 6 credits, so the main images render at 1K with true alpha and get placed onto a pure-white canvas as a separate step — which also guarantees the "no text, no logo, no watermark on the hero" rule, since the hero is just the product.</p></div>
            </div>
            <div itemscope itemprop="hasPart" itemtype="https://schema.org/Question" style="margin-bottom:24px;">
                <h3 itemprop="name" style="color:#f9fafb;font-size:1.05rem;margin:0 0 8px;">Q: Is it cheaper to translate listing images or regenerate them per language?</h3>
                <div itemprop="acceptedAnswer" itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer"><p style="color:#d1d5db;margin:0;">Editing is about four times cheaper. Translating 24 infographics into three extra marketplaces as flat-6 image edits (Grok 2.0 edit) costs 432 credits; regenerating all 72 as fresh 24-credit Pro renders costs 1,728 — and re-rolls the approved product pixels, restarting review. Localization is a genuine image-editing problem, not a re-generation one.</p></div>
            </div>
            <div itemscope itemprop="hasPart" itemtype="https://schema.org/Question" style="margin-bottom:24px;">
                <h3 itemprop="name" style="color:#f9fafb;font-size:1.05rem;margin:0 0 8px;">Q: How long should a main product video be, and what does it cost?</h3>
                <div itemprop="acceptedAnswer" itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer"><p style="color:#d1d5db;margin:0;">Around eight seconds — long enough for one idea, short enough that per-second billing stays sane. An 8-second draft on Seedance 2 mini 720p is 15/s (120), the shipped final on Kling V3 Turbo image-to-video 720p is 27/s (216). Five hero-SKU finals total 1,080 credits; the marketplace caps useful listing-video length well below what a longer cut would cost, so seconds are the lever.</p></div>
            </div>
            <div itemscope itemprop="hasPart" itemtype="https://schema.org/Question" style="margin-bottom:24px;">
                <h3 itemprop="name" style="color:#f9fafb;font-size:1.05rem;margin:0 0 8px;">Q: What does a full four-marketplace listing month cost end to end?</h3>
                <div itemprop="acceptedAnswer" itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer"><p style="color:#d1d5db;margin:0;">Twelve SKUs with complete image sets, 72 localized overlay edits, five hero videos with drafts, and 18 localized voice-over tracks: 3,624 list credits — 2,971 at Basic 82%, 2,645 at Pro 73%, 2,282 at Ultra 63%. The correct shape: the still-image and localization lines carry the catalog, and video is the premium layer you pay for only on the hero SKUs.</p></div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section itemprop="articleSection" style="margin-bottom:0;">
            <h2 style="color:#f9fafb;border-bottom-color:#374151;">Closing: The Catalog Scales by Edits, Not by Re-Shoots</h2>
            <p style="color:#d1d5db;">A twelve-SKU, four-marketplace launch ships because two decisions were made at template time rather than at the last minute: dense text gets a resolution floor it will not be argued out of, and localization is treated as an edit to an approved master instead of a fresh generation. The invoice is what that discipline looks like priced — 3,624 list credits a month, the whole localization effort carried by a 432-credit edit line that would have been 1,728 the lazy way, and a video premium spent only where it moves conversion. The lanes run inside <a href="https://www.fuseaitools.com/home/qwen/v3-pro-text-to-image" style="color:#60a5fa;text-decoration:none;">Qwen 3 Pro</a>, <a href="https://www.fuseaitools.com/home/kling/v3-turbo-image-to-video" style="color:#60a5fa;text-decoration:none;">Kling V3 Turbo</a>, and their neighbors on FuseAI — try the overlay-edit lane on one already-approved infographic first; watching it change only the text is the fastest way to see why the re-shoot reflex is the most expensive line you will never put on the sheet. Try <a href="https://www.fuseaitools.com/home/gpt-image/v2-5-flare-text-to-image" style="color:#60a5fa;text-decoration:none;">FuseAITools</a> for white-background ecommerce listing images.</p>
