            <p style="color:#d1d5db;margin-top:16px;">Discounts are the monthly plan rates: Basic 82%, Pro 73%, Ultra 63%, applied per line and rounded, and the columns sum to the total. Two readings of the shape. The staging line alone is <strong style="color:#f9fafb;">1,080 — 28% of the month</strong> — because virtual staging prices per room and rooms are the unit of inventory; a desk that stages three rooms per listing has a different business than one that stages eight. And the motion stack: two Hailuo lines totaling 1,200 on flat-per-clip menu pricing, 540 on per-second teasers where shortness is the policy, and 160 of audio that behaves exactly as predicted. Real estate is the vertical where <strong style="color:#f9fafb;">the still-image factory and the video factory cost about the same</strong> — 1,920 vs 1,740 — which is what a market built on photographs looks like priced.</p>
